tasks.brief:
Fix the single bug in /tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/pricing.ts. The doc comment says pct is a whole percentage: applyDiscount(1000, 10) === 900. The function currently does Math.round(cents * (1 - pct)), which treats 10 as 1000% and returns -9000.

Change only this line:
return Math.round(cents * (1 - pct));
to:
return Math.round(cents * (1 - pct / 100));

Leave subtotal, tax, the interface, and the doc comment as they are. Do not edit t2/test/pricing.test.ts or any other file. Do not run tests or any shell commands.

Fix the single bug in /tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/inventory.ts. The doc comment says reserve takes qty units if that many are left and returns whether it did. Stock starts as A1=3, B2=0, C3=12. The guard is `if (have <= qty) return false`, which rejects taking the exact remaining quantity (reserve('A1', 3) returns false).

Change only this condition:
if (have <= qty) { return false; }
to:
if (have < qty) { return false; }

Leave inStock, the stock map, and the doc comment as they are. Do not edit t2/test/inventory.test.ts or any other file. Do not run tests or any shell commands.

Fix the single bug in /tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/checkout.ts. The doc comment says checkout reserves every sku and throws 'out of stock <sku>' when one can't be reserved, then returns the cart total. The loop currently does `if (!reserve(sku, qty)) { continue; }`, which skips a failed reserve and still returns the total. The test expects checkout of B2 qty 1 to throw an error matching /out of stock B2/.

Change only this line:
if (!reserve(sku, qty)) { continue; }
to:
if (!reserve(sku, qty)) { throw new Error('out of stock ' + sku); }

Leave the function signature, imports, and doc comment as they are. Do not edit t2/test/checkout.test.ts or any other file. Do not run tests or any shell commands.

